From 6663139423bd5bb3615e6e02c170ebd1f99a0738 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 19:47:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(cron): keep monitor changes pending until a successful
 agent run acknowledges them [daveey]

Five whys (hub cron 6b4342ad83d9, 2026-11-14 14:52:18): a monitor change was
never reported because (1) the agent never ran: SubscriptionQuotaUnavailable
refused agent construction; (2) the next ticks saw unchanged output and
suppressed the agent; (3) check_monitor persisted the new hash + snapshot at
detection time, BEFORE the agent ran; (4) so detection, not handling, was the
state boundary; (5) nothing owned redelivery of a detected-but-unhandled change.
All eight lifecycle=empty warnings in the hub agent logs follow quota errors.

Fix: a durable per-job outbox (cron/monitor_outbox.py) in
job["monitor_state"] (outbox_version 1):
- check_monitor runs the source first (a source error stages nothing), then,
  under the jobs-store lock, queues each changed observation as a generation
  {id, old, new, hash, first_run, attempts} chained off the acknowledged
  snapshot (last_output/last_output_hash) and offers the OLDEST pending one with
  its stable change id. Snapshots live inline in jobs.json, so staging and
  acknowledgement are one atomic save_jobs write (temp + fsync + replace).
- Acknowledgement is generation-bound: only the head generation with the same id
  is consumed, so a late/stale ack can never drop a newer observation (B pending,
  C observed, B acked -> C offered next with a B->C diff).
- The owner's run_job acknowledges right after the agent returns, before output
  save and notification delivery: blank, incomplete (incl. max-iteration
  handoff), interrupted and [CRON_FAILURE] answers keep it pending; [SILENT]
  counts as success; a delivery failure never replays a handled change. Every
  agent path (gateway firer, restart-safe external worker, direct) converges on
  that owner run_job.
- _apply_monitor_gate clears any stale _monitor_change_id first, so only the
  generation offered this tick can be acknowledged.
- Retries are observable: attempts counter in state, MonitorOutcome.attempt, and
  a WARNING "re-offering unacknowledged change <id> (attempt N)".
- discard(job_id, change_id, reason) is a distinct, generation-bound operator
  path recording last_discard.
- Corrupt/missing state fails visibly as a monitor source error (schema,
  version, chain, hashes, ids, types, missing job, missing/undecodable legacy
  snapshot). Legacy hash-only state migrates from monitor_last_output.txt.
- Delivery is at-least-once; the change id in the prompt lets consumers dedupe.
No quota routing policy change.

Tests (RED first, then GREEN): tests/cron/test_monitor_outbox.py (replay after
restart, successive generations + stale ack, corruption matrix, discard, missing
job/snapshot, retry observability, crash after staging in a real subprocess,
failed staging write, stale change-id fence), tests/cron/test_monitor_kind.py
(real run_job/owner: pre-agent typed quota failure -> source error -> original
diff retried -> success -> suppressed, for baseline and A->B; unsuccessful
results retain; success/[SILENT] consume), tests/cron/test_monitor_outbox_worker.py
(real _run_external_worker_payload -> run_one_job -> owner run_job: quota
failure keeps A->B, success with failed delivery acknowledges, next fire
suppressed; killed by a no-ack mutant). Consumers migrated:
test_gated_tick_clears_gate_streak.py, test_redact_telegram_boundary.py.
